From b91e8dbd9f14644f1353e320f777746dc2c04163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnikoopour <7692789+rnikoopour@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:54:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] prompt cache: key kept states by image content, so image
 prompts resume

The cache matched kept states by token ids alone, and every image's span is
its placeholder token repeated, so any request holding an image skipped the
cache: a long chat with one picture re-read its whole context every turn and
held the lane's GPU for minutes.

- Image.key: a digest of the span length and prepared payload (server)
- the server computes history_len for image prompts too (placeholders
  widened to their spans in the rendered history)
- LaneHost.cacheTokens: the prompt as the cache matches it, each image
  span's positions holding ids past the vocabulary drawn from the image's
  key and the position in the span; unkeyed images still skip the cache
- dsv41: kept states restore for image prompts, keeps happen at their marks,
  and spans wholly inside the restored rows skip the vision tower and the
  rank-1 row transfer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
